          These five cards carried <img> tags pointing at picsum.photos: random
          stock photographs fetched from a third party on every view of a
          product page, each with alt text describing something the photograph
          did not contain ("A web application open in a browser" over whatever
          that seed happened to return). A visitor got a third-party request
          they did not ask for, and a screen reader got a description of an
          image nobody had ever looked at.

          Real art here wants real product screenshots, which is a design and
          content decision rather than something to invent in passing. Until
          those exist, a token-driven band keeps the cards' proportions and
          claims nothing. It is decorative, so it is aria-hidden and the
          heading and paragraph carry the whole meaning. --}}
